- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** The measured data moves out of `data.zip` into the optics-mueller kit byte for byte, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads it there, read-only, through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (001 §Q AT-1 'the CSV entries of `data.zip` into `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` … `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` is then deleted, with its `Content` link in `BerremanTests.fsproj` … There is no second copy of the data' and 'The CSVs are read through the existing `MuellerDataStore` parser (`parseMuellerCsv`, the "Phone ROI CSV" import profile)'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable'; 001 §G 'The two committed reference kits … are read-only to tests'; .spec-md §3.12, §3.20, §3.21 and §7 'moved byte-for-byte … There is no second copy'; the S9.4 brief). After this step nothing reads `data.zip`; the archive-keyed seam the tests stop using is retired in step 331. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) Byte for byte. The lab CSVs are CRLF text, all but `cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` with a UTF-8 byte-order mark, and the catch-all `* text=auto eol=lf` (`.gitattributes:9`) would store them as LF, so a clone would hold other bytes than the archive and than the SHA-256 a kit records at attach (001 §E). `.gitattributes` therefore gains, after its last rule, a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S9.4 (lab files are kept exactly as recorded) and the rule `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/** -text !eol`, the form of its `*.nb` rule (`.gitattributes:58`). `AGENTS.md`'s 'Line endings: LF' gotcha (`AGENTS.md:513-516`) gains one sentence: the lab files under `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` are the exception, kept byte for byte by that rule (spec 0050 S9.4), and are never converted. (2) The move. Each entry of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` is written with the bytes the archive holds: each CSV to `data/optics-mueller/` joined with its archive path, so `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` becomes `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` and the eight exploratory CSVs land in `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/`; and each of the three `data/shapes/*.json` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` under its own name. Before the archive is deleted, each written file's SHA-256 is checked against its entry's (the values in (4)). Then `data.zip` is deleted, with the folders `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` and `Berreman/Data/` it leaves empty. `BerremanTests.fsproj` loses the `ItemGroup` holding the `data.zip` `Content` link and its comment (`BerremanTests.fsproj:52-62`), and the comment above the `OpticalConstructor.Storage` `ProjectReference` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:88-90`), which names `createFileBacked`, gone since spec 0044, and the contract that step 331 retires; the reference stays, because the tests read the parser, the folder `KitProxy` and the Phone ROI CSV profile from Storage. The README (`data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`, step 329) describes the data where it now is, in its own voice: the opening paragraph says the measured data is this kit's lab files under `data/raw/`; the paragraph after the provenance table says the lab files live in this kit, that `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads them read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (`MuellerDataStore.parseMuellerCsv`), and that no code path references the external checkout; the provenance sentence on line endings says the scripts and summaries were converted to LF while the lab CSVs keep their recorded bytes; the `Measured data` table's row is `data/raw/`, the lab files moved byte for byte out of the former `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` by spec 0050 S9.4; and the inventory says the folder holds 15 CSVs, seven of them the science data under `data/raw/final/` (the table's entries, now kit paths, keep their texts), the other eight earlier exploratory work under `data/raw/`, and that the archive's three beam-shape descriptions are in `data/reference/shapes/`. Every other line keeps its text. (3) The locator (.spec-md §3.21). New `Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs` in `namespace BerremanTests`, compiled directly before `MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` (one `<Compile>` line in `BerremanTests.fsproj`, no comment): `type CommittedKit = | OpticsMuellerKit`, the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4 and saying that S10.2 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`; and `member this.tryFindFolder : KitFolder option`: from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, each folder upward in turn until one holds `Berreman/Berreman.slnx`, which is the repository root; the answer is `KitFolder (FolderName <root>/data/optics-mueller)` (`KitFolder`, step 122) when that folder exists, and `None` when no folder upward holds the solution or the kit folder is absent. It writes nothing and reads no environment variable. No other case, member or file is added; AT-2's kit adds its case when S12.2 commits that kit. (4) The reads, in `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`. `loadDataSet` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:loadDataSet`) becomes `loadDataSet (file : KitRelativePath) : MuellerRawRow list`: `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, then `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView.readDataFile file` (steps 126, 128 and 131: a read-only view writes nothing, not even `.oc/`), then `(BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile).mapText` (step 303) of the file's `text`, answering its `CapturePoints` rows; no kit folder, a `KitError`, an `ExperimentDataError` or another `MappedPoints` case fails the test with what it says, as the helper fails today. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4. The seven data sets become test-local `KitRelativePath` values bound ahead of the members, each born by `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123) of its kit path, an `Error` failing the test: `lpLpFile` `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv`, `lpCplFile` `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv`, `cplLpFile` `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv`, `cplCplDay1File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv`, `cplCplDay2File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv`, `darknessChecksFile` `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv`, `bullshitChecksFile` `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv`, the mapping `MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName` holds. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` and `section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly` drop `MuellerDataStore.createArchiveBacked ()`, bind `load` to `loadDataSet` and load each data set's file in place of its case (`load LpLpFamily` becomes `load lpLpFile`, …); every comment of theirs that names the archive store names the kit's lab files, and their bodies and assertions are otherwise unchanged. `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` becomes `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts`: through `loadDataSet`, `lpLpFile` 209, `lpCplFile` 209, `cplLpFile` 209, `cplCplDay1File` 170, `cplCplDay2File` 57, `darknessChecksFile` 6, `bullshitChecksFile` 2 rows, its comment naming the inventory of `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md` (spec 0042 §6). New fact `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`: through `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView` over `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, `readDataFile` of each of these kit paths answers a file whose `contentHash` is the `ContentHash` (step 24) of its former archive entry's hex SHA-256: `data/raw/cpl_cpl.csv` `c1cbbde1c7b77acf6d23f972bb85f679e0072779d396a49aaf02b1d92e447eb5`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_big_center.csv` `515d16bb7a375b734038a8dbc6730bb6e726d99bfd11d954b986adf81d47b7b8`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_center.csv` `f2d97088f562cb5e8097b827b6774d1ba88baefd25b15f312515ad77b958d703`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_small_center.csv` `aa18398266782f7cedf15008a8e66beff28f89c81304d68e062d6f8f8216c78b`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_standard_ellipse.csv` `94b8ef01770a12617f55e1b329d1513670044cee3c0c5e340e9c5826588372e5`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_095.csv` `59a7b7d7f223bf28c4623299df6a530f63787570eb346935b76d468228fbd3bc`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_105.csv` `4fd5b0b5fc09cd291d57732edfd1f582c37119c230c7550d100ebd4a94493336`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` `53de707ce70b9792d024db41ae39eac8506656916c97b0db1ef9f1512ef50813`; `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv` `f2f7d28d881b57f5760562d030c12d1e554c7c8cc82d6657e9e4fb5c281c2c9e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv` `9920ae4768558bd865c0190878adf97dde9901e9436a299a0c49e7d48ed39664`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv` `fcace7c401940d6b4a84347acd2b2afb925f5ea9c2c57e64fcc6d88e4ad26b2e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv` `9737ebe6534446ce3d4e1bcbcda222b88fae2d3c58de0cc8db1d322a5c002f39`; `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv` `3b11f42dd67f29a09275b13442849415c82d7a967f5d5933713abb06dfb43cc2`; `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv` `d014c90144a98eb1949d30716be1f01049ec9763e0e3b94ceb68d2e43c4b1ba8`; `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` `0fc29a63fd7de90b85842af5020cd79fb1e74ac2d24b49f7c7673cbead82cd81`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_095.json` `f8b15f8069d4986c6a68924349c66b0455b7a976da441adfdf5620af3d9e9425`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_105.json` `e254c679a2861bf5f625a03b5d62c2e6a6f3aac38f29afdfba632521370bedeb`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_v1.json` `76bb56c20c63356640ad286f1f1b109eaa9714f7ea16c2606086705d88854f2d`. The class doc's first sentence names the Phone ROI CSV parser in place of 'the archive-backed `MuellerDataStore`', and its spec 0044 §8 bullet on `data.zip` says the measured data is the optics-mueller kit's lab files, found from the repository root and read read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0050 S9.4); its other bullets keep their text. The trailing comments of the two `open OpticalConstructor.Storage…` lines are deleted. `muellerCsvFixture`, `malformedMuellerCsv`, `the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)` and `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw` are unchanged; the mock data proxy, its three facts and the two `tryLoadFromArchive` facts, which read no archive file, go with the seam in step 331.

**Acceptance.** After the lab files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` MUST hold the fifteen CSVs and `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` the three shape files, each byte for byte its former `data.zip` entry under the `-text !eol` rule, `Berreman/Data/` and the `data.zip` `Content` link MUST be gone, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read the kit's lab files read-only through the Phone ROI CSV profile from the repository root; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged, `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` renamed `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts` and `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte` added, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.
